WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.436 --> 00:00:05.825
"Is my only option to do it on my own?"

00:00:05.825 --> 00:00:10.768
So I have a great question from one of my YouTube viewers, Jeremy, who wrote in to say:

00:00:10.768 --> 00:00:15.429
"Hello, Evan! Great video, as always! You're my favorite guru!" Thanks, Jeremy...

00:00:15.429 --> 00:00:19.292
"I need help, I have an idea for recording a short drama/music video, but I don't know anyone

00:00:19.292 --> 00:00:22.910
"reliable enough who has the creativity or understanding to help me shoot the video

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:25.983
and I don't have the funds to hire a professional videographer or crew."

00:00:25.983 --> 00:00:29.741
"What can I do? Is my only option to do it all on my own?"

00:00:29.741 --> 00:00:31.026
Jeremy...

00:00:31.026 --> 00:00:34.151
welcome to the world of entrepreneurship! Right?

00:00:34.151 --> 00:00:39.567
We NEVER have the resources we need to make our vision happen.

00:00:39.567 --> 00:00:44.877
And entrepreneurs, the difference... what makes a successful entrepreneur is you find a way.

00:00:44.877 --> 00:00:49.782
You find a way to bootstrap this thing up and make your dream happen

00:00:49.782 --> 00:00:55.686
when all logical things say: "this is never going to happen." Ok?

00:00:55.686 --> 00:00:57.925
So here are some options for you. You want to make this video happen?

00:00:57.925 --> 00:01:00.186
Here are a few options you can try:

00:01:00.186 --> 00:01:02.052
First off: Get a clear vision.

00:01:02.052 --> 00:01:06.760
Ok? I would research other videos, other productions that you've looked at, that you like,

00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:10.452
and try to identify the elements of those videos that you really like. Right?

00:01:10.452 --> 00:01:14.397
There's tons of videos online, go to YouTube, start your search.

00:01:14.397 --> 00:01:18.464
Pull out elements and make a list. Let's say: "You know? From 10 seconds to 20 seconds

00:01:18.464 --> 00:01:24.929
I really like how they do this..." So the more specific you can get, the better.

00:01:24.929 --> 00:01:31.785
Second thing is: Go out and start networking with people who believe in the same thing as you.

00:01:31.785 --> 00:01:34.015
I don't know what this video's all about, right?

00:01:34.015 --> 00:01:37.873
You need to do a good job with explaining the big vision behind it.

00:01:37.873 --> 00:01:42.052
Why are you doing this? Why is it so important to you? What big thing are you trying to accomplish?

00:01:42.052 --> 00:01:46.735
Because if your video stands for something that has meaning, that is going to have an impact on this world,

00:01:46.735 --> 00:01:50.680
then people will want to be a part of it, but you have to explain what you're doing.

00:01:50.680 --> 00:01:57.603
So, for example, I like to salsa dance, ok? And recently, this morning, a salsa band wrote to me,

00:01:57.603 --> 00:02:02.841
they're launching a new song and they're bringing in people from around the world

00:02:02.841 --> 00:02:08.653
and they're asking them: "can you please dance on camera to all or part of the song?

00:02:08.653 --> 00:02:14.524
"Because we want to make a music video combining all the dancers from around the world with our song."

00:02:14.524 --> 00:02:19.327
So it's a pretty cool project and it's a nice song, so I'm thinking of going with my dance partner to Toronto Island

00:02:19.327 --> 00:02:24.090
so I can film the CN Tower behind and I'll dance to the song and hopefully be part of their video.

00:02:24.090 --> 00:02:28.403
Why am I doing this? I'm doing this for free, right? I've got to take time to go to Toronto Island,

00:02:28.403 --> 00:02:33.415
travel there, come up with, you know, whatever I'm going to dance to; it's going to take like the whole

00:02:33.415 --> 00:02:35.636
day to do this. Why am I willing do to this?!

00:02:35.636 --> 00:02:39.382
Because it's fun. Because it's different. Because it's going to have an impact.

00:02:39.382 --> 00:02:41.925
And it's free, right? I'm not getting paid to do this.

00:02:41.925 --> 00:02:47.865
So, people will join your cause if they feel like they're doing something important; so, explain it. Right?

00:02:47.865 --> 00:02:51.089
And start hanging around people, networking online, offline;

00:02:51.089 --> 00:02:55.201
with people who can potentially help you in the video space. Ok?

00:02:55.201 --> 00:03:02.039
Number 3, though, is: Don't let the lack of a video editor hold you back.

00:03:02.039 --> 00:03:03.898
Get started.

00:03:03.898 --> 00:03:07.522
Because too many times entrepreneurs are launching a product and they say:

00:03:07.522 --> 00:03:12.470
"Oh, I finally have this and I can make it", or "until I get the funding", or "until I get the partner",

00:03:12.470 --> 00:03:14.555
or "until I get the sponsorship, I'm not going to do anything."

00:03:14.555 --> 00:03:17.232
That's not how it works!

00:03:17.232 --> 00:03:20.614
You've got to start creating momentum. You've got to start building this thing up.

00:03:20.614 --> 00:03:23.302
And it may mean you do the whole thing yourself,

00:03:23.302 --> 00:03:29.322
but start! Don't let the lack of resources or capital, or people, or ideas hold you back

00:03:29.322 --> 00:03:31.936
from getting this thing done. Because this is only one project, man.

00:03:31.936 --> 00:03:38.812
You've got a long future ahead of you, of great things. This is one project to kick you off.

00:03:38.812 --> 00:03:44.456
So 1: research, do your homework; background, find all the elements that you love that you want to include.

00:03:44.456 --> 00:03:48.728
2: make this thing important. Start hanging out and introducing it to people who

00:03:48.728 --> 00:03:51.979
are in the video space, who may be able to help you out.

00:03:51.979 --> 00:03:57.461
And then 3: just get started. Do something every day to make this thing go a little bit further

00:03:57.461 --> 00:04:03.563
and don't let the lack of anything hold you back, because what entrepreneurs are great at is turning nothing,

00:04:03.563 --> 00:04:09.322
turning an idea, into something special.This is your first challenge.

00:04:09.322 --> 00:04:10.877
Believe!

00:04:10.877 --> 00:04:13.557
For those of you watching, I'd love to hear what you have to think.

00:04:13.557 --> 00:04:17.857
How did you find the people, the resources to make your first idea happen?

00:04:17.857 --> 00:04:22.193
Leave it in the comment section below. I'm curious to learn and it's also going to help inspire other people,

00:04:22.193 --> 00:04:24.180
so leave it below.

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:26.781
You liked this video? Give it a thumbs up, it makes me want to do more for you.

00:04:26.781 --> 00:04:29.611
And click on my face to subscribe to the channel to see more videos like this.

00:04:29.611 --> 00:04:32.718
Thank you so much! I'll see you soon.

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:40.000
